{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Domain requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is valid.\n\n- **Placement:** The citation sits in fenced commentary on an explicit function with a body, so the function-level exception is allowed.\n- **Substance:** The reason is specific, not just \"hard to cover\". `Domain` requires `node_content`. `StoredGraph` is a storage-only fixture whose tests delegate `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` through `node_path` alone. The function body is a deliberate `panic!` guard that rejects any content read, so running it would break the test's own invariant.\n- **Agreement with the source:** The tests that use `StoredGraph` (`consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` and `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`) call only `node_path`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`. The `StoredReview` criterion's `execute` never reads contents. So the guard is not expected to run, and the commentary matches the code.\n- **Other fixtures:** The claim that other graph fixtures exercise content resolution is true. The `Domain` implementations in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs` (`impl[Memory/Domain]`), `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` (`impl[Application/Domain]`) and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` (`impl[Memory/Domain]`) return real content and record reads.\n\nThe item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to the same target, so there is no redundancy. I found no gap.",
